==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ped-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|quadrupède}}, from {{uder|en|frm|-}}, from {{uder|en|la|-}} stem of {{m|la|quadrupēs||four-footed, a four-footed animal}}, from {{m|la|quadri-||four-}} + stem of {{m|la|pes||foot}}. Alternatively analyzable as {{confix|en|quadri|alt1=quadru|ped}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkwɒdɹəpɛd/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-quadruped.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[four-footed]] or [[four-legged]] [[animal]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 February 22|author=Stephen Roberts|title=Reading... between the lines... to Wales|journal=RAIL|issue=977|page=56|text=Bradshaw knew nothing of the 'wind of change' that was coming in a century's time, so he contented himself with an exposition on the Vale of the White Horse, "deriving its singular denomination from the gigantic carving of that useful '''quadruped''', on a high chalky hill beyond".}}
# A [[mammal]] [[ambulating]] [[on all fours]].

